# A call of a mounted service's method is one serializable transaction on
# each store it uses: it commits when the method succeeds and rolls back when
# it fails. The fixture's board serves `move_task`, which reads a card, checks
# the version the caller saw, waits, and writes the next version. Two
# concurrent calls on one version give one move and one Conflict, because
# the later call's read waits for the earlier call's commit. A method that
# writes and then fails leaves the card as it was. A mounted method may use a
# store at all: it is checked with no effect bound, as a route handler is.
fixture: write_method_is_one_serializable_transaction.fixture
env: NO_COLOR=1
env: JET_STORE_DIR={work}/cache
step: jet run main.jet
exit: 0
stdout: = write_method_is_one_serializable_transaction.stdout.expected
